 "notes": [
  "No single reproduce.py is shipped: verify_claims.py asserts every reported number against a fresh recomputation, and each section is regenerated by its own script in code/.",
  "CTransPath logits are included for all three datasets and were regenerated with the corrected ConvStem extraction under scikit-learn 1.6.1.",
  "The paper reports the fixed-base general-vision results (code/general_vision_fixedbase.py); general_vision.py is retained for comparison.",
  "CKA values reported in the paper are full-sample computations. The shipped 2,000-row subsets reproduce them to within the subsampling standard deviation of 0.003-0.006; see results/cka_uncertainty.json.",
  "CTransPath logits are included for all three datasets, regenerated with the corrected ConvStem extraction under scikit-learn 1.6.1.",
  "The paper reports the fixed-base general-vision results (code/general_vision_fixedbase.py); general_vision.py is retained because the difference between the two designs is itself reported in Section 6.",
  "Three values from earlier drafts (held-out fusion 63.68%, pooled gain +2.99, dose-response slope +0.278) were taken from stored files rather than recomputed; they are superseded by 57.37%, +2.97 and +0.094 respectively, and are now covered by the verification harness. See README.",
  "v5: packaging and documentation fixes only; no reported number changed. See the 'Changes in this revision of the archive (v5)' table in README.md."
 ],
